<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<pnml xmlns="http://www.pnml.org/version-2009/grammar/pnml">
  <net id="SEQ-06b" type="http://www.pnml.org/version-2009/grammar/ptnet">
    <name><text>06b Competitive bidding under the New Government Procurement Act (RA 12009): who does what, with the time limits</text></name>
    <page id="page1">
      <place id="p1"><name><text>start</text></name><initialMarking><text>1</text></initialMarking></place>
      <place id="p2"><name><text>p2</text></name></place>
      <place id="p3"><name><text>p3</text></name></place>
      <place id="p4"><name><text>p4</text></name></place>
      <place id="p5"><name><text>p5</text></name></place>
      <place id="p6"><name><text>p6</text></name></place>
      <place id="p7"><name><text>p7</text></name></place>
      <place id="p8"><name><text>p8</text></name></place>
      <place id="p9"><name><text>p9</text></name></place>
      <place id="p10"><name><text>p10</text></name></place>
      <place id="p11"><name><text>p11</text></name></place>
      <place id="p12"><name><text>p12</text></name></place>
      <place id="p13"><name><text>p13</text></name></place>
      <place id="p14"><name><text>p14</text></name></place>
      <place id="p15"><name><text>p15</text></name></place>
      <place id="p16"><name><text>p16</text></name></place>
      <place id="p17"><name><text>p17</text></name></place>
      <place id="p18"><name><text>p18</text></name></place>
      <place id="p19"><name><text>p19</text></name></place>
      <place id="p20"><name><text>p20</text></name></place>
      <place id="p21"><name><text>p21</text></name></place>
      <place id="p22"><name><text>p22</text></name></place>
      <place id="p23"><name><text>p23</text></name></place>
      <place id="p24"><name><text>end</text></name></place>
      <place id="p25"><name><text>p25</text></name></place>
      <place id="p26"><name><text>p26</text></name></place>
      <transition id="t01"><name><text>1. Requesting office to BAC and procurement unit: Purchase request, specifications, bidding documents for an item in the Annual Procurement Plan</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t02"><name><text>2. BAC and procurement unit to Budget unit: Are appropriations available for this procurement?</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t03"><name><text>3. Budget unit to BAC and procurement unit: Confirmation: the item is in the budget law, or in the proposed budget for early procurement</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t04"><name><text>4. BAC and procurement unit: Pre-procurement conference: the procurement follows the plan, appropriations are available, the award criterion is chosen</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t05"><name><text>5. BAC and procurement unit to PhilGEPS (modernized): Post the invitation to bid and the bidding documents, with the budget for the contract and the source of funding. Also on the website of the entity, and 7 days at its premises</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t06"><name><text>6. PhilGEPS (modernized) to Suppliers and payees: Notice visible to registered suppliers</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t07"><name><text>7. BAC and procurement unit to Suppliers and payees: Pre-bid conference, at least 12 days before the deadline for bids (required from a budget of PHP 3 million)</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t08"><name><text>8. Suppliers and payees to BAC and procurement unit: Bids in two sealed envelopes: technical (with eligibility documents and bid security) and financial. Deadline: at most 45 days (goods), 50 or 65 (works), 75 (consulting) after posting</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t09"><name><text>9. BAC and procurement unit to Observers: Invitation to observe each stage: at least two observers, in addition to the representative of COA</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t10"><name><text>10. BAC and procurement unit: Opening of bids immediately after the deadline. Each envelope passes or fails. A bid above the approved budget for the contract is rejected</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t11"><name><text>11. BAC and procurement unit: Bid evaluation: 7 days for the lowest calculated bid, 14 days when quality is rated with price, 21 days for consulting. Rank by the award criterion</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau1"><name><text>enter: Until one bidder passes, starting from the first in rank</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t12"><name><text>12. BAC and procurement unit to Suppliers and payees: Post-qualification within 12 days: verify the legal, technical and financial documents, with the latest tax returns</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau2"><name><text>repeat</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau3"><name><text>exit the loop</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t13"><name><text>13. BAC and procurement unit to Head of agency: Recommendation of award, with the document that authorizes the entity to incur the obligation</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t14"><name><text>14. Head of agency to Suppliers and payees: Approval within 10 days, then the notice of award immediately</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t15"><name><text>15. Head of agency to PhilGEPS (modernized): Award published</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t16"><name><text>16. Suppliers and payees to Head of agency: Performance security, before signing: 5 percent (goods, consulting) or 10 percent (works) of the contract price, 30 percent as a surety bond</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t17"><name><text>17. Head of agency to Suppliers and payees: Contract signed within 10 days from receipt of the notice of award</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t18"><name><text>18. Head of agency to Suppliers and payees: Notice to proceed within 3 days from approval of the contract</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t19"><name><text>19. Observers to Head of agency: Observation report (also to PhilGEPS, and copies to the GPPB and the Ombudsman)</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t20"><name><text>20. Observers to COA: Observation report</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau4"><name><text>skip: A losing bidder objects</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t21"><name><text>21. Suppliers and payees to BAC and procurement unit: Request for reconsideration within 3 days. The BAC decides within 7 days</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t22"><name><text>22. Suppliers and payees to Head of agency: Protest within 7 days, filed electronically, with a fee that is not returned. Decision within 7 days. It is final for smaller contracts. For the others: review by the Regional Trial Court</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau5"><name><text>end of: A losing bidder objects</text></name></transition>
